      "content": "thanks, that's a decent start. but to really win a debate at this level, i can't just know the general themes; i need to know the actual substance they'll use to try and corner me. \n\ncould you go deeper into that second point? specifically, what are the actual \"scientific\" frameworks or specific genetic theories they lean on to argue that these differences aren't just environmental? like, if i'm in the middle of a cross-examination, i need to know the specific logic they use to claim that cognitive traits are tied to evolutionary selective pressures in different geographic regions. what's the most sophisticated version of that argument?",
